1	// Acceptance tests for the change request:
2	//   "Let me put labels on projects so I can group them."
3	//
4	// A project now carries LABELS (tags). Opening a project (project-open-<id> from the projects list)
5	// reaches its detail page, which shows a tags region (project-tags) holding that project's labels in
6	// a list (project-tags-list) — one chip per label (project-tag-<id>, keyed by the TAG's id) showing
7	// the label's name. Labels are shared, first-class things ("so I can GROUP them"): the SAME label can
8	// sit on more than one project, and it shows on each project it is attached to — while a label that is
9	// not on this project does not appear here.
10	//
11	// A form adds a label to the project: type the label name into project-tag-add and submit it with
12	// project-tag-add-submit — the label then appears as a chip in the list. Each chip offers a control to
13	// take the label back off the project (project-tag-remove-<id>). Attaching a label appends exactly one
14	// audit record — PROJECT_TAGGED project=<project> tag=<tag> — and detaching one appends exactly one
15	// PROJECT_UNTAGGED project=<project> tag=<tag>, so the grouping change can be checked back later (the
16	// UI only shows the current labels; it cannot show that one was just attached or removed).
